{"title":"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23bff7d9649b742e2a9d22cfce5c3eb891697184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b1bb8663e4a744dc1c459290af22a3b3eaae05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> be  concentric circles, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b1bb8663e4a744dc1c459290af22a3b3eaae05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> in the interior of  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23bff7d9649b742e2a9d22cfce5c3eb891697184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. From a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23bff7d9649b742e2a9d22cfce5c3eb891697184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> one draws the tangent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b1bb8663e4a744dc1c459290af22a3b3eaae05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c5d1bf526c8d98272f4a3fd8df629570bd0c6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B\\in {\\cal C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the second point of intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23bff7d9649b742e2a9d22cfce5c3eb891697184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. A line passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b1bb8663e4a744dc1c459290af22a3b3eaae05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\cal C}_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in such a way that the perpendicular  bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> intersect at a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Find, with proof,  the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83531a4c13b687601c8e55f86b2bf7412fe1db9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM/MC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c00566cb3564ce68d5fabce265995c97d438f5a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  unitsize(1.5 cm); path p = circle((0,0),1); path q = circle((sqrt(2)/2,1),3sqrt(2)/2); pair[] x = intersectionpoints(p, q); pair O,A,B,C,D,E,F,M1,M2,M; O = (0,0); A = (-2sqrt(2),1); B = (0,1); C = (2sqrt(2),1); D = (A+B)/2; E = x[0]; F = x[1]; M1 = (D+E)/2; M2 = (C+F)/2; M = (D+C)/2; draw(p); draw(q, dashed); draw(circle((0,0),3)); draw(A--C--F--A); draw(D--E); draw(C--F); draw(M1--M--M2); dot(O); dot(E); dot(F); dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(D); dot(M); dot(M1); dot(M2); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NW); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,SW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,SW); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,N); label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,S);  [/asy]\" width=\"445\" height=\"435\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/139b53c2eaba2e052998971be962ab5f625ec048.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=\\frac{AB}{2}=\\frac{AC}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"140\" height=\"38\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> all lie on a circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf225c2bfb8b5670f5b270311a27e718fa1063e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE \\cdot AF=AB \\cdot AB=\\frac{AB}{2} \\cdot 2AB=AD \\cdot AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"364\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc92b2c96c9759e3433d5566fedf4e6d32cb6765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACF \\sim \\triangle AED$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d11a3d7b31e99ca6c2e35198cb15019b24931c7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACF = \\angle AED$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/1/14154cc012ea8d03c7d7d367674d6306b264a102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CFED$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> is cyclic, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> must be the center of the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/1/14154cc012ea8d03c7d7d367674d6306b264a102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CFED$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />, which implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa1b1f09e837a362f6af6c2b4f67639814607137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC=\\frac{CD}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"90\" height=\"37\" />. Putting it all together,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03ce9e0d5c7ed6ffbc56bb1a14691a200867cf91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AM}{MC}=\\frac{AC-MC}{MC}=\\frac{AC-\\frac{CD}{2}}{\\frac{CD}{2}}=\\frac{AC-\\frac{AC-AD}{2}}{\\frac{AC-AD}{2}}=\\frac{AC-\\frac{3AC}{8}}{\\frac{3AC}{8}}=\\frac{\\frac{5AC}{8}}{\\frac{3AC}{8}}=\\boxed{\\frac{5}{3}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"612\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>Borrowed from <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://mks.mff.cuni.cz/kalva/usa/usoln/usol982.html\">https://mks.mff.cuni.cz/kalva/usa/usoln/usol982.html</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will use signed lengths. WLOG let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5c76d295875eedec88e18c0a7ef4ab99266460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f86ce0ad24da08336d28ac26230f15c8bb9e72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = x$\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/b/c2b21c92d36dcb9127bbf9ed8f6c8985ff5c398e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = y &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/7676bb86e9162142043f19c0502c5bf05e69f5dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 2$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0784975d4b8be997f4dfdeb77135b8ffc032bce6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f71844a1213cbd9ca0af1e940f3c22eeb332b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM = x - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/632f6dfa6381a36f4b9025de68b129b0a5a923b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC = 4 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"99\" height=\"13\" />. By Power of a Point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bb1b40929242031c02cffc8440aa1411915053f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE \\cdot AF = AB^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"162\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/5/1e5e8c053c71cea6dcc26968d41d83a651d7b0cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = \\frac{4}{AE} = \\frac{4}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/5315a8273e0e76574dc40e3b15845331d13153d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF = \\frac{4}{y} - y = \\frac{4 - y^2}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"177\" height=\"44\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is on the perpendicular bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/0/550850fc2645a1d18b9499b92abe7b51b88d887e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|DM| = |EM| = |x - 1|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9095292a2c207eaf90595cc68032c5703377bc6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|CM| = |FM| = |4 - x|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>By Stewart's Theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/959ad44e9829be5a3aea0cb7164d5722016421b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MFA$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and cevian <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5d96c8d1e481244e028c9e97d1d7b53206536b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b1778acaa1f4808c7bfe633904dd9d79af8647ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4}{y}(y(\\frac{4-y^2}{y}) + (x-1)^2) = y(4-x)^2 + \\frac{4-y^2}{y} \\cdot x^2;\\]\" width=\"394\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b9714380e013085f61dfa0c44724444e4ce21c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4(4 - y^2 + (x-1)^2) = y^2(4-x)^2 + (4-y^2)x^2;\\]\" width=\"367\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3f0f0ba782e94e79f337ae04f902d4f77f9c46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16 - 4y^2 + 4x^2 - 8x + 4 = x^2y^2 - 8xy^2 + 16y^2 + 4x^2 - x^2y^2;\\]\" width=\"472\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e03e04c3ee55b1ea5dea3503db902e6d6d8ecc21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8xy^2 - 8x- 20y^2 + 20 = (8x - 20)(y^2 - 1) = 0.\\]\" width=\"373\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>So either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6f1c411db1f2fcea56a9ae422ef5ef80cc5c687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8x - 20 = 0$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fd165217c17456797cd264c937460b671a6054c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 - 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fd165217c17456797cd264c937460b671a6054c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 - 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b19312092289bfb754a592ec62937f3bba34d52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = y = 1 = AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"148\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb29d28dc277d3f98fb410ade6e23c00540bbec8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = AC = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />, so the perpendicular bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> are the same line, and they do not intersect at a point. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c302b7d098bca0fbf99fb64c1c67fa4dfe315bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = x = \\frac{5}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"103\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/0/6f06fe4b0d6b8f8cff09742f4fc7a20069b7f7e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC = \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac8cf335446e322571f807cb044304435c12b58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AM}{MC} = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"87\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO\" title=\"1998 USAMO\">1998 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017121324\nCache expi